  "description": "Shift into climbing mode with a wireless drivetrain and a wider gear ratio.\n\nBuilt for big days in the mountains off the beaten track, where the all-terrain geometry of our fastest gravel frame meets the unrivaled shifting performance of a SRAM Rival/Eagle hybrid transmission. Ideal for ultra races and high-elevation riding.\n\nSram DUB | Road Wide | T47 85.5mm\n\nSRAM Rival | Gravel disc brake\n\nSRAM XS-1270 Eagle Transmission | 10-52T | 12s\n\nSRAM GX Eagle Transmission Flattop | 12s\n\nSRAM Rival XPLR | 40Z | 172,5mm\n\nSRAM Rival AXS / GX Eagle Transmission 1x12\n\nTout Terrain Gravel Fork | carbon fork\n\nTout Terrain EX-F1 | Centerlock rotor interface\n\nFizik Microtex Performance grip tape\n\nRitchey VentureMax | 420mm (S, M) / 460mm (L, XL)\n\nAcros | EC34 / EC34\n\nSRAM GX Eagle Transmission AXS | 1x12 T-Type\n\nTout Terrain EX-R1 - 10/11/12S | Centerlock rotor interface\n\nTout Terrain | 70mm | +/- 6°\n\nCeres steel frame | Tout Terrain Thermocrom tubing\n\n4 (frame) + 2 (fork)",
